    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter the final day of August with a lineup optimized for high-contact efficiency and opportunistic base-running. Our strongest play of the day is **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an 81.88 score. His matchup against T. Gordon is bolstered by a favorable park factor and a 100% stolen base expectation against a slow-delivering pitcher, allowing him to maximize both power and efficiency in the 3-hole. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (73.39) also provide elite value, benefiting from substantial platoon advantages that elevate their output against their respective right-handed matchups. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top-tier starters with a 70.50 score; his top-of-the-order positioning combined with a strong xwOBA profile makes him our primary engine for Runs today.\n\nWhile we are missing major production from **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to scheduling off-days, our depth remains tested. **Sam Antonacci** (60.88) narrowly earned a starting nod in the outfield, primarily due to his leadoff role and platoon edge against P. Lambert. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where we ultimately kept **Nasim Nunez** (56.26) in the starting lineup over other depth options. Despite batting 8th, **Nasim Nunez** provides critical scarcity value in stolen bases; his 88% probability of success against the pitcher's delivery pace makes him a mathematical necessity for our 5x5 Roto structure, outweighing the raw power potential of bench alternatives.\n\nThe roster is largely healthy, though we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined, and **Andy Pages**, who is officially on the IL. We are proceeding with **Liam Hicks** (55.38) and **Coby Mayo** (54.85) despite moderate scores, as the scarcity of their respective positions dictates usage regardless of slightly tougher opposing SP_xERAs. With **Miguel Vargas** and **Wade Meckler** providing serviceable baselines, the goal for today is to leverage the speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Sam Antonacci** to close the gap in our most competitive category. Keep a close watch on the weather and late lineup changes, as our reliance on dynamic platoon splits makes us highly sensitive to defensive adjustments from opposing managers.",
